<section class="section faq on-light" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="wrap faq-grid"><div class="faq-intro"><h1 class="h2" id="faq-title">A few things you might be wondering</h1><p class="lead">Still have a question? The ATH team can help you find the right next step.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item"><summary>Who can apply to the programme?</summary><p>The programme is for students currently enrolled at an institution in Abia State who want to explore or build a startup idea.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do I need to have a finished product?</summary><p>No. You can apply with an early idea or with something you have already started. The application asks about the problem, your approach and what you hope to learn.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How long is the incubation programme?</summary><p>The programme runs for six weeks, combining practical training with mentorship as you develop and test your idea.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What should I prepare before applying?</summary><p>Be ready to share your contact and study details, explain the problem you want to solve, describe your idea and tell us where you would value support.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can I save my application and finish later?</summary><p>Yes. Your draft is saved on the device you are using. You can return to it later and review your answers before submitting.</p></details></div></div></section>
